and are amortized on a straight-line basis over their estimated useful lives of 5 years. Property and equipment acquired in the acquisition is depreciated over its estimated remaining useful life.","context":"The excess purchase consideration allocated to goodwill primarily represents the value attributable to the assembled workforce, expected synergies, future growth opportunities, and other intangible benefits that do not qualify for separate recognition. Of the total goodwill recognized, approximately $88,000 was attributable to the assembled workforce and approximately $102,000 represented residual goodwill.","section":"Business Combination","block":311,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001437749-26-027665","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001644903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1644903/000143774926027665/ycbd20260630_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a0d8db48447df5a1fcd5ef0641220a00f6f7fda725a892479c7b5eb58fcd7332.bin","sha256":"a0d8db48447df5a1fcd5ef0641220a00f6f7fda725a892479c7b5eb58fcd7332"}},{"id":"5d079013bd6dae35557a7159b8a8ec7ab78469eae87afe06d0179157b3132428","quote":"The Company has continued to pursue several potential acquisitions since the conversion of the Series A Preferred Stock in 2025. In January 2026, the Company acquired the Bluebird brand. The Company believes Bluebird provides (i) a large existing customer base that is underserved with its existing product portfolio (ii) a brand name not defined by CBD, allowing for natural expansion into other natural products, (iii) significant SG&A synergies, and (iv) intellectual property including self-GRAS status on their full spectrum product. During the second quarter of fiscal 2026, the acquisition cost and integration costs created a $75,000 drag on the P&L, and an additional $24,000 in costs in the third quarter related to the accounting valuation. Bluebird contributed over $550,000 in revenue for the third quarter of fiscal 2026.","context":"Toward the end of the first quarter of 2026, the Company raised additional cash to bolster its balance sheet with the Series C Preferred Stock and structured an ELOC. Over the last few months, we have seen several instances where the stock price and volume have increased and we believe the ELOC will allow us to prudently take advantage of these situations should they occur in the future.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS.","block":338,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001437749-26-027665","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001644903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1644903/000143774926027665/ycbd20260630_10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a0d8db48447df5a1fcd5ef0641220a00f6f7fda725a892479c7b5eb58fcd7332.bin","sha256":"a0d8db48447df5a1fcd5ef0641220a00f6f7fda725a892479c7b5eb58fcd7332"}},{"id":"a3e52901c570ad0bb69642d744499100043bea65926333f6bd3b8e3408856bf9","quote":"On June 26, 2026 the Company issued 100,000 shares of common stock under the ELOC for gross proceeds of $61,990. The shares were issued under the exemption from registration provided by Section 4(a)(2) of the Securities Act.","context":"Except as disclosed below, there were no unregistered sales of the Company’s equity securities during the period covered by this report, that were not previously disclosed in a Current Report on Form 8-K.","section":"ITEM 2. UNREGISTERED SALES OF EQUITY SECURITIES AND USE OF PROCEEDS.","block":433,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001437749-26-027665","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001644903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/da